cuems-common (1.3.0-12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * cuems-node-engine.service: order After=olad.service. On a controller
    (which runs both olad.service and node-engine, and node-engine spawns
    cuems-dmxplayer) there was no ordering between them, so at cold boot the
    player could start before olad.service bound 127.0.0.1:9010 and spawn a
    rogue default-config olad that squats the port. olad.service then failed
    with 'Address already in use', the Eurolite MK2 never registered, and DMX
    stayed dead until manual recovery. Pure ordering (not Requires/Wants): a
    no-op on nodes where olad isn't enabled, a wait-for-olad on controllers.
  * cuems-ola-profile: add eurolite-mk2 profile. Eurolite USB-DMX512 PRO MK2
    presents as a stock FTDI FT232R (0403:6001) and is claimed by the usbdmx
    EurolitePro factory. The profile enables usbdmx, auto-detects the connected
    FT232R serial from sysfs and pins eurolite_mk2_serial, and disables the
    conflicting ftdidmx/usbserial/stageprofi plugins.

