cuems-common (1.3.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Network interfaces: stop shipping /etc/network/interfaces as a conffile (it
    is host- and role-specific) and replace the obsolete dpkg-divert +
    interfaces.cuems mechanism. On FIRST install only, postinst takes over
    /etc/network/interfaces with a reachable baseline
    (/usr/share/cuems/interfaces.master), preserving any pre-existing file (e.g.
    the debian-installer default) at .dpkg-old; on upgrades it is never touched
    (operator / clone / role-template config wins). This is necessary because a
    stock Debian interfaces names the original NICs, which our .link files
    rename to ethernet0/ethernet1/wifi0 -- the stock file would otherwise go
    stale and drop the network. Role templates (interfaces.master /
    interfaces.node) still ship under /usr/share/cuems/. The old diversion is
    removed cleanly (without --rename, leaving the live file as-is) and the
